@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Prepared execution boundary
+
+`feathered_app.prepared_plan.BuildPlan` owns one run's mutable graph. Construction
+copies options, inventories, repository records, source-policy metadata and
+mirror publication options together, preserving internal aliases but separating
+caller-owned objects and other runs. Repository verification fields remain
+mutable: metadata acquisition legitimately annotates them. Root requests become
+immutable `RootRequest` values without losing pins, architecture, repository or
+source identity. Picked-package identities become a frozen set.
+
+This intentionally strengthens direct construction. A caller can no longer
+modify the original options or repository objects after passing them to a plan
+and thereby alter that run. Use the plan's owned objects to inspect execution
+annotations. Normal GUI/CLI preparation already copied substantial state; the
+change does not claim that those paths previously lacked isolation.
+
+The legacy `feathered_app.build_runner.BuildPlan` import and constructor argument
+order remain supported. `PreparedPlan` is a union of three concrete plan types,
+with RPM, Debian and Arch inventory parameterizations kept distinct. It is not
+a plan whose inventory slot can silently switch among those families.
+
+`execution_feedback` binds reporting, cancellation, decisions, transfer-plan
+notification and terminal events through `BuildFeedbackHost`. The checked
+implementation includes mirror progress mapping and source-qualified item
+identities. Terminal tuples, warning collection and decision defaults retain
+their existing behavior. Each binding creates its own reporter state. The core
+reporter now requires only an `is_set()` cancellation capability rather than a
+particular threading class.
+
+The new modules and build outcomes are checked with strict optional handling,
+complete function annotations, generic parameters and return-value checks.
+The host-contract gate accepts the concrete implementations and rejects mixed
+inventory assignments and malformed root/repository/feedback inputs.
+
+This is a completed vertical slice of implementation instruction 6, not a claim
+that the entire application host is typed. The runner's source/catalog/output
+host remains broad, and backend extraction (instruction 7) is deferred until
+artifact and event characterization covers all three families. No resolver,
+trust policy, repository display URL or bundle schema is rewritten here.
