+## Current build-boundary batch
+
+This batch starts at upstream `b14bf5e0de840269289e5c2e728f1e17e26c39a7`.
+The unmodified source passed 1,341 local tests with no skips or deselections.
+Baseline and focused evidence are in `validation/build-boundary/`; current
+full-tree evidence is in `validation/build-boundary-gate/`. Earlier reports in
+`validation/release-gate/`, `item1/` and `batch25/` are historical evidence.
+
+New coverage checks direct plan ownership, all three inventory types, ordered
+execution feedback, cancellation and terminal outcomes. A real GUI build is
+compared with a CLI replay for exact payload hashes, selected identities,
+source-policy records, provenance (excluding its generated ID and creation
+instant), and installer bytes. Existing Tk-blocked, native-family orchestration,
+mirror, GUI locking and replay tests remain in the complete release gate.
+See `BUILD-BOUNDARY.md` for the typing and compatibility scope.
+
+GitHub run 34737027821 on the baseline passed its native APT/DNF/pacman and static
+analysis jobs but failed the Windows Python/Tk bootstrap before application tests.
+Only its exit-code annotation was publicly available during this review; detailed
+job log access returned HTTP 403. This batch does not claim to fix or certify
+that bootstrap. A local Linux pass does not establish Windows release readiness.
+
 ## Scope of local validation
 
 The follow-on batch implements instruction items 2-5: credential-safe display
@@ -78,7 +100,7 @@ with source URLs visible, strict decoding of recognized spec fields and runtime
 preparation inputs, partial-outage recovery, shared release-knowledge ownership,
 and bounded UI event processing with incremental query coordination. Each
 behavioral repair has focused regression evidence in `validation/batch25/`;
-the complete final-tree result remains `validation/release-gate/SUMMARY.md`.
+the complete final-tree result remains `validation/build-boundary-gate/SUMMARY.md`.
 Malformed specs formerly accepted by truthiness are intentionally rejected;
 valid older specs and incomplete drafts remain supported. See
 `BACKGROUND-REFRESH.md` for cache ownership, cancellation and migration scope.
